{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDE4L0Jpc2JlZSUyMCUyNzE3JTIwJTI4MjAxOCUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"Bisbee '17","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/u2mtK0C7dIlzigxyNZGxw3z3AKF.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/2iZUXxID84ppNl6ZaTRffWJV9x4.jpg","description":"It’s 2017 in Bisbee, Arizona, an old copper-mining town just miles from the Mexican border. The town’s close-knit community prepares to commemorate the 100th anniversary of Bisbee’s darkest hour: the infamous Bisbee Deportation of 1917, during which 1,200 striking miners were violently taken from their homes, banished to the middle of the desert, and left to die. Townspeople confront this violent, misunderstood past by staging dramatic recreations of the escalating strike. These dramatized scenes are based on subjective versions of the story and “directed,” in a sense, by residents with conflicting views of the event. Deeply personal segments torn from family history build toward a massive restaging of the deportation itself on the exact day of its 100th anniversary.\n\nRated NR · Released 5 Sept 2018 · United States of America · Language: English · 124 min\nStudio: Impact Partners, Concordia Studio, Doc Society\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2018","genres":["Documentary","History","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.9","runtime":"124 min","cast":["Fernando Serrano","Laurie McKenna","Graeme Family","Mike Anderson","Richard Hodges","James West"],"director":["Robert Greene"],"released":"2018-09-05T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"The past is present.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Robert Greene","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/lvmcOBo5isNQJkpivaJa2Zkmw9N.jpg"},{"name":"Fernando Serrano","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/lW60y7UbZw5Y6veXDQZS3Vc5TeD.jpg"},{"name":"Laurie McKenna"},{"name":"Graeme Family"},{"name":"Mike Anderson"},{"name":"Richard Hodges"},{"name":"James West"}]},"trailers":[{"source":